-- Lesson 2 step by step (IELTS-02 v1.1.0): five guided steps and one mixed check on the lesson's passage, in the
-- Lesson 6 format (LEARN FIRST worked example, an explanation for every answer). Owner instruction 2026-10-28 00:10
-- (Asia/Bishkek): put every lesson in steps like Lesson 6, starting with the Reading lessons.
-- Named-student pilot with requires_review; nothing is released. Source: docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_READING_07.json.
-- The lesson passage is written once (art) and appended to each step's LEARN FIRST text; stored content equals the source.
do $steps$
declare art constant text := '

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

THE PASSAGE: A quiet place after school

A. For a four-week pilot in April, Westbrook School opened a quiet study room on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday afternoons, from 3:30 to 5:00. The room had sixteen seats. Students needed to book by noon on the day they wanted to attend. They could use the school''s website or ask the office to make the booking on paper.

B. The idea came from students who shared busy rooms at home and wanted somewhere with fewer distractions. Before the pilot, eleven students answered a short survey. Eight preferred a quiet room, while three wanted a space for group discussion. The school chose to test the quiet room first. Students could bring homework or read their own books, but they could not hold group conversations there.

C. At the end of the pilot, staff planned to ask students which features had helped them study. The pilot did not measure examination results. Staff had not yet decided whether to offer longer opening hours.';
begin
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r34-v1','0.1.0','Lesson 2 step 1 of 6: What must you check?','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then, for each claim, choose the kind of detail that decides the answer. Do not read the passage yet.','Every claim has one detail that decides it: a number, a day or time, who, all or only some, a reason, or a future decision. Find that detail first.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "Claim: ''The room was set up because the library was too noisy.'' What must you check?", "accepted_answers": ["E"], "taxonomy_node_id": "29a67bc9-2c34-42e6-9f5f-a8b592f7bb3b", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a number"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a day or time"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  who did it"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  all or only some"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  a reason (why)"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  a future decision"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Claim: ''The head teacher suggested the quiet room.'' What must you check?", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "29a67bc9-2c34-42e6-9f5f-a8b592f7bb3b", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a number"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a day or time"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  who did it"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  all or only some"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  a reason (why)"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  a future decision"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "Claim: ''Twenty students answered the survey.'' What must you check?", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "29a67bc9-2c34-42e6-9f5f-a8b592f7bb3b", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a number"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a day or time"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  who did it"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  all or only some"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  a reason (why)"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  a future decision"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "Claim: ''Staff will add Friday sessions next month.'' What must you check?", "accepted_answers": ["F"], "taxonomy_node_id": "29a67bc9-2c34-42e6-9f5f-a8b592f7bb3b", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a number"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a day or time"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  who did it"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  all or only some"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  a reason (why)"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  a future decision"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Claim: ''The room stayed open until six o''clock.'' What must you check?", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "29a67bc9-2c34-42e6-9f5f-a8b592f7bb3b", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a number"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a day or time"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  who did it"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  all or only some"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  a reason (why)"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  a future decision"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Claim: ''Students could use the room only for homework.'' What must you check?", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "29a67bc9-2c34-42e6-9f5f-a8b592f7bb3b", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a number"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a day or time"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  who did it"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  all or only some"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  a reason (why)"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  a future decision"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS preparation exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 6, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-reading-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 E, a reason (why). ''Because'' introduces the reason. Check whether the text gives the same reason.\n2 C, who did it. The claim names a person, the head teacher. Check who the text says had the idea.\n3 A, a number. ''Twenty'' is the detail; you will compare it with the number in the text.\n4 F, a future decision. ''Will add'' says a decision has been made. Check whether the text says anything was decided.\n5 B, a day or time. ''Until six o''clock'' is a time. The room and opening are only the topic.\n6 D, all or only some. ''Only'' limits the claim. If the text allows anything else, ''only'' makes the claim FALSE.\nRead each explanation, then find the proof in the passage yourself.", "focus": "Select relevant information: identify the detail in a TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN claim that must be checked against the text."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: find the detail that decides the answer

A TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN claim has a TOPIC (what it is about) and one DETAIL that decides the answer. The topic helps you find the place in the text. The detail is what you check.

Six kinds of detail come up again and again:
- a number (how many, how long)
- a day or time (when)
- who did it (a person or a group)
- all or only some (every, all, only, most, some)
- a reason (because, so that, why)
- a future decision (will, plans to, has decided)

WORKED EXAMPLE
Claim: ''The club meets on Tuesday.''
Topic: the club''s meeting. Detail: ''Tuesday'', a day.
So you look for the day in the text. If the text says Thursday, the answer is FALSE.

Now name the deciding detail in six new claims about a school study room.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_READING_07.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'e79317b99b1d56285a8aa177865a843b606bd12e49ce3a66e46bf47a360c7771',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r35-v1','0.1.0','Lesson 2 step 2 of 6: Find the right place','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then choose the paragraph that has the information you need to check each claim.','Match the meaning of the claim, not its words. Find the sentence you would use as proof.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "Which paragraph do you need to check this claim: ''Some students wanted to work in groups''?", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "Paragraph A"}, {"value": "B", "label": "Paragraph B"}, {"value": "C", "label": "Paragraph C"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Which paragraph do you need to check this claim: ''Students were asked for their opinion after the trial''?", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "Paragraph A"}, {"value": "B", "label": "Paragraph B"}, {"value": "C", "label": "Paragraph C"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "Which paragraph do you need to check this claim: ''The room could hold sixteen people at most''?", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "Paragraph A"}, {"value": "B", "label": "Paragraph B"}, {"value": "C", "label": "Paragraph C"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "Which paragraph do you need to check this claim: ''Group conversations were not allowed in the room''?", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "Paragraph A"}, {"value": "B", "label": "Paragraph B"}, {"value": "C", "label": "Paragraph C"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Which paragraph do you need to check this claim: ''The trial took place in spring''?", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "Paragraph A"}, {"value": "B", "label": "Paragraph B"}, {"value": "C", "label": "Paragraph C"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Which paragraph do you need to check this claim: ''The opening hours might become longer''?", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "fc8a9d7e-3fe4-48a4-9325-84b193ee747c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "Paragraph A"}, {"value": "B", "label": "Paragraph B"}, {"value": "C", "label": "Paragraph C"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS preparation exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 7, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-reading-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 Paragraph B: \"three wanted a space for group discussion\". Work in groups = group discussion.\n2 Paragraph C: \"At the end of the pilot, staff planned to ask students\". After the trial = at the end of the pilot.\n3 Paragraph A: \"The room had sixteen seats.\" Seats tell you how many people the room could hold.\n4 Paragraph B: \"they could not hold group conversations there\". The rules for the room are in B, not in A.\n5 Paragraph A: \"For a four-week pilot in April\". Spring is a paraphrase of the month, April.\n6 Paragraph C: \"Staff had not yet decided whether to offer longer opening hours.\" Might become longer = had not yet decided whether to offer longer hours.\nRead each explanation, then find the proof in the passage yourself.", "focus": "Locate specific detail: find the paragraph that holds the evidence for a claim before deciding TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: find the proof before you decide

Before you decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN, find the sentence that the claim is about. Look for the same MEANING, not the same words.

- Paragraph A gives the facts of the pilot: when, where, how many seats, how to book.
- Paragraph B gives the background: where the idea came from, the survey and the rules.
- Paragraph C looks ahead: what staff planned and had not decided.

WORKED EXAMPLE
Claim: ''Students could book a place by phone.''
Booking is a practical fact, so start in A. Proof: "They could use the school''s website or ask the office to make the booking on paper."
The place to check is Paragraph A. (Then you would decide: the text gives two ways, and the phone is not one of them.)

Now find the paragraph for six claims.' || art),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_READING_07.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'cad5b338e901eca240dc04ea196c4db6251a9186f4992b1999a92a635361fb5c',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r36-v1','0.1.0','Lesson 2 step 3 of 6: TRUE or FALSE?','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then decide whether each claim agrees with the passage (TRUE) or says the opposite (FALSE). Every claim in this step is TRUE or FALSE.','TRUE means the same meaning in different words. FALSE means the passage says something that cannot be true at the same time as the claim.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "The room was open on three afternoons a week.", "accepted_answers": ["TRUE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Bookings could only be made online.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "The pilot ran for a whole school term.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "Fewer than half of the students surveyed wanted a discussion space.", "accepted_answers": ["TRUE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Students were allowed to read books that were not for school.", "accepted_answers": ["TRUE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "The school tested a group discussion room before the quiet room.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS preparation exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 8, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-reading-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 TRUE. Proof: \"Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday afternoons\". Three named afternoons = three afternoons a week.\n2 FALSE. Proof: \"or ask the office to make the booking on paper\". A second way to book means ''only online'' is wrong.\n3 FALSE. Proof: \"a four-week pilot\". Four weeks is much shorter than a term.\n4 TRUE. Proof: \"three wanted a space for group discussion\". Three of eleven is fewer than half.\n5 TRUE. Proof: \"read their own books\". Their own books = books that were not for school.\n6 FALSE. Proof: \"The school chose to test the quiet room first.\" The order is the opposite of the claim.\nRead each explanation, then find the proof in the passage yourself.", "focus": "Locate specific detail: decide whether a claim agrees with or contradicts the text, recognising paraphrase."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: same meaning or opposite meaning?

TRUE: the passage gives the same information, usually in different words.
FALSE: the passage gives information that cannot be true at the same time as the claim. You can point to the words that make the claim wrong.

Look for paraphrase. Different words can have the same meaning, and similar words can have a different meaning.

WORKED EXAMPLE 1
Claim: ''Sessions ended at five o''clock.''
Proof: "from 3:30 to 5:00". 5:00 = five o''clock.  -> TRUE

WORKED EXAMPLE 2
Claim: ''Students had to bring their own chairs.''
This step has no claims like this one: the passage says nothing about chairs, so it would be NOT GIVEN. You will practise NOT GIVEN in step 4.

Now decide TRUE or FALSE for six claims.' || art),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_READING_07.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'3720bbf3dabfbf87daa46e2f70dd848091160e3b81c05ac3f11b17ae8f70c24d',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r37-v1','0.1.0','Lesson 2 step 4 of 6: FALSE or NOT GIVEN?','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked examples. Then decide whether each claim is contradicted by the passage (FALSE) or not answered by it (NOT GIVEN). Every claim in this step is FALSE or NOT GIVEN.','FALSE needs words in the passage that say the opposite. If the passage is silent, even about a topic it mentions, the answer is NOT GIVEN.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "Students had to book their place a day in advance.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "The quiet room was in the school library.", "accepted_answers": ["NOT GIVEN"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "Most of the survey answers came from older students.", "accepted_answers": ["NOT GIVEN"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "Staff had already agreed to longer opening hours.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "The pilot compared the exam results of students who used the room with those who did not.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Students who booked on paper were given the first seats.", "accepted_answers": ["NOT GIVEN"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS preparation exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 8, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-reading-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 FALSE. Proof: \"book by noon on the day they wanted to attend\". On the same day, not a day before.\n2 NOT GIVEN. The passage never says where the room was. The library is not mentioned at all.\n3 NOT GIVEN. The passage gives the number of students (eleven) but not their ages.\n4 FALSE. Proof: \"Staff had not yet decided whether to offer longer opening hours.\" Not yet decided is the opposite of already agreed.\n5 FALSE. Proof: \"The pilot did not measure examination results.\" It could not compare results it did not measure.\n6 NOT GIVEN. Paper booking is mentioned, but nothing is said about who got seats first. The topic is there; the information is not.\nRead each explanation, then find the proof in the passage yourself.", "focus": "True/False/Not Given reasoning: separate a contradicted claim from one the text does not answer."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: opposite, or silent?

This is the hardest choice in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN.
- FALSE: you can copy words from the passage that say the opposite.
- NOT GIVEN: the passage does not tell you. The topic may be there, but the information is not.
Do not use your own knowledge or guesses. Ask: can I point to the words?

WORKED EXAMPLE 1
Claim: ''The room had twenty seats.''
Proof: "The room had sixteen seats."  -> FALSE (sixteen, not twenty)

WORKED EXAMPLE 2
Claim: ''A teacher was always present in the room.''
The passage never says who supervised the room. You cannot point to any words.  -> NOT GIVEN

Now decide FALSE or NOT GIVEN for six claims.' || art),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_READING_07.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'bf843e86f55edc98362316623a574121037b295949f5cd2555dd070a3c6d9747',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r38-v1','0.1.0','Lesson 2 step 5 of 6: Small words, big differences','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then choose TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. Check the small word in each claim first.','Small words (only, all, most, some, never, always, because) change what a claim says. Check them before anything else.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "Students could use the room only for homework.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Some of the students surveyed wanted a place for discussion.", "accepted_answers": ["TRUE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "The room was always fully booked.", "accepted_answers": ["NOT GIVEN"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "Students were never allowed to say anything in the room.", "accepted_answers": ["NOT GIVEN"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Most of the students surveyed preferred a quiet room.", "accepted_answers": ["TRUE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Because the pilot was popular, the school decided to open the room for longer.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS preparation exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 8, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-reading-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 FALSE. Proof: \"Students could bring homework or read their own books\". Reading their own books was also allowed, so ''only'' is wrong.\n2 TRUE. Proof: \"three wanted a space for group discussion\". Three students = some of them.\n3 NOT GIVEN. The passage gives the number of seats and the booking rule, but never says how many seats were booked.\n4 NOT GIVEN. The rule is about group conversations (\"they could not hold group conversations there\"). The passage does not say whether a quiet word was allowed. ''Never ... anything'' goes beyond the text.\n5 TRUE. Proof: \"Eight preferred a quiet room\". Eight of eleven is most of them.\n6 FALSE. Proof: \"Staff had not yet decided whether to offer longer opening hours.\" No decision had been made, for any reason.\nRead each explanation, then find the proof in the passage yourself.", "focus": "True/False/Not Given reasoning: check limiting and absolute words (only, all, most, never, always, because)."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: check the small words

Small words can change the whole meaning of a claim:
- only, all, every, never, always: very strong. One exception makes them FALSE; if the passage is silent, NOT GIVEN.
- most, some: check the numbers. Eight of eleven is ''most''; three of eleven is ''some''.
- because: the reason must be the one the passage gives.

WORKED EXAMPLE
Claim: ''Every student in the survey wanted a quiet room.''
Proof: "Eight preferred a quiet room, while three wanted a space for group discussion."
''Every'' is wrong: three students wanted something else.  -> FALSE

Now check six claims. Circle the small word first.' || art),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_READING_07.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'827fb7dde023a290855b5ae17eba4ca83fa9ebdef0528ca0991dd94b45642feb',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r39-v1','0.1.0','Lesson 2 step 6 of 6: Mixed check','reading','independent_check','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then answer six new questions: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. Work on your own, without notes, a dictionary or help. Tell your teacher if anything interrupted you.','Use the whole routine: find the deciding DETAIL, LOCATE the sentence by meaning, then decide: same meaning, opposite meaning, or silent.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "The quiet room was tried out for about a month.", "accepted_answers": ["TRUE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Eight of the students surveyed wanted a discussion space.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "The office could make bookings for students who did not use the website.", "accepted_answers": ["TRUE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "Students who used the room said that it helped them study.", "accepted_answers": ["NOT GIVEN"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Students could come to the room without booking if there were free seats.", "accepted_answers": ["FALSE"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "The room was more popular than the school had expected.", "accepted_answers": ["NOT GIVEN"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "bcddba69-28bc-436c-bb54-01a3c5733099", "options": [{"value": "TRUE", "label": "TRUE"}, {"value": "FALSE", "label": "FALSE"}, {"value": "NOT GIVEN", "label": "NOT GIVEN"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS preparation exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 8, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-reading-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 TRUE. Proof: \"a four-week pilot\". Four weeks = about a month.\n2 FALSE. Proof: \"Eight preferred a quiet room, while three wanted a space for group discussion.\" Eight wanted the quiet room; only three wanted discussion.\n3 TRUE. Proof: \"or ask the office to make the booking on paper\".\n4 NOT GIVEN. Staff \"planned to ask students which features had helped them study\". A plan to ask is not an answer.\n5 FALSE. Proof: \"Students needed to book by noon on the day\". Booking was required.\n6 NOT GIVEN. The passage says nothing about how many students came or what the school expected.\nRead each explanation, then find the proof in the passage yourself.", "focus": "True/False/Not Given on one passage, with paraphrase, limiting words and claims the text does not answer."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: the whole routine

1. DETAIL: what decides the claim? (number, time, who, all/only/some, reason, future)
2. LOCATE: find the sentence with the same meaning.
3. DECIDE: same meaning = TRUE. Opposite meaning you can copy = FALSE. Nothing in the passage = NOT GIVEN.

WORKED EXAMPLE
Claim: ''The room was open in the mornings.''
Detail: a time (mornings). Locate: Paragraph A, "Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday afternoons, from 3:30 to 5:00".
Decide: afternoons, not mornings.  -> FALSE

Now answer six new questions on your own.' || art),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_READING_07.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'7b27ccf5a42c1fdeea93e7e8d5f873626e000ae936cb2eea9165acd93af32675',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
end $steps$;
